, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm hoping someone can help with a problem I've run into. The end goal is to get mavsdk_server running on my Jetson Nano. Then I'll use MAVSDK JavaScript to interface with a simulator (and then ultimately real hardware) from a web page. I've been following the instructions here:\r\n\r\nhttps://mavsdk.mavlink.io/v0.24.0/en/contributing/build.html\r\n\r\nto build for my Jetson Nano. I've gotten close with the following commands:\r\n\r\n`docker run --rm dockcross/manylinux2014-aarch64 > ./manylinux2014-aarch`\r\n\r\n`./dockcross-manylinux2014-aarch64 cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_MAVSDK_SERVER=ON -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -Bbuild/manylinux2014-aarch64 -S.`\r\n\r\nFrom here: https://hub.docker.com/r/dockcross/manylinux2014-aarch64\r\n\r\nBut then I ultimately end up with the following error:\r\n\r\n[ 83%] Linking CXX static library libabsl_synchronization.a\r\n[ 83%] Built target synchronization\r\ngmake[3]: *** [all] Error 2\r\ngmake[2]: *** [absl/src/absl-stamp/absl-build] Error 2\r\ngmake[1]: *** [CMakeFiles/absl.dir/all] Error 2\r\ngmake: *** [all] Error 2\r\n**CMake Error at third_party/cmake/build_target.cmake:50 (message):\r\n  /work/build/manylinux2014-aarch64/third_party/absl failed to build!**\r\nCall Stack (most recent call first):\r\n  third_party/CMakeLists.txt:23 (build_target)\r\n\r\n-- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!\r\nSee also \"/work/build/manylinux2014-aarch64/CMakeFiles/CMakeOutput.log\".\r\n\r\nI've done some digging around in the GitHub issues and see a couple of references to absl, but I'm not 100% certain where to go from here. My compilation is being done on my MacBook using the main branch.\r\n\r\nI'd also like to point out that building the linux-arm7 variant as mentioned in the documentation does work. \r\n\r\nAny insight would be very much appreciated.\r\n\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "dbaldwin", "id": 38339, 